WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:00.880
All right, my friends.

00:00.880 --> 00:06.440
So, so far in the bronze layer and in the silver layer, we didn't discuss anything about the business.

00:06.440 --> 00:08.800
So the bronze and silver were very technical.

00:08.800 --> 00:10.760
We are focusing on data ingestion.

00:10.760 --> 00:13.920
We are focusing on cleaning up the data quality of the data.

00:13.920 --> 00:17.240
But still the tables are very oriented to the source system.

00:17.240 --> 00:22.760
Now comes the fun part and the gold layer where we're going to go and break the whole data model of

00:22.760 --> 00:23.480
the sources.

00:23.480 --> 00:29.000
So we're going to create something completely new to our business that is easy to consume for business

00:29.000 --> 00:30.640
reporting and analysis.

00:30.640 --> 00:35.000
And here it is very important to have a clear understanding of the business and the processes.

00:35.000 --> 00:40.480
And if you don't know it already at this phase, you have really to invest time by meeting maybe process

00:40.480 --> 00:46.160
experts, the domain experts, in order to have clear understanding what we are talking about in the

00:46.160 --> 00:46.600
data.

00:46.600 --> 00:51.120
So now what we're going to do, we're going to try to detect what are the business objects that are

00:51.120 --> 00:53.040
hidden in the source systems.

00:53.080 --> 00:54.960
So now let's go and explore that.

00:55.000 --> 00:55.320
All right.

00:55.360 --> 01:00.120
Now in order to build a new data model I have to understand first the original data model.

01:00.120 --> 01:04.360
What are the main business objects that we have, how things are related to each others.

01:04.400 --> 01:07.680
And this is very important process in building a new model.

01:07.680 --> 01:11.480
So now what I usually do I start giving labels to all those tables.

01:11.480 --> 01:14.880
So if you go to the shapes over here let's go and search for label.

01:14.920 --> 01:19.050
And if you go to more icons I'm gonna go and take this label over here.

01:19.050 --> 01:23.290
So drag and drop it, and then I'm going to go and increase maybe the size of the font.

01:23.330 --> 01:25.730
So let's go with 20 and bold.

01:25.730 --> 01:27.330
Just make it a little bit bigger.

01:27.330 --> 01:33.410
So now by looking to this data model we can see that we have a product informations in the CRM and as

01:33.410 --> 01:34.330
well in the ERP.

01:34.370 --> 01:38.050
And then we have like customer informations and transactional table.

01:38.050 --> 01:39.770
So now let's focus on the products.

01:39.770 --> 01:42.290
So the products information is over here.

01:42.290 --> 01:45.410
We have here the current and the history product informations.

01:45.410 --> 01:48.530
And here we have the categories that belong to the products.

01:48.530 --> 01:51.370
So in our data model we have something called products.

01:51.370 --> 01:52.850
So let's go and create this label.

01:52.850 --> 01:54.370
It's going to be the products.

01:55.090 --> 01:57.690
And let's go and give it a color to the style.

01:57.730 --> 02:00.210
Let's pick for example the red one.

02:00.210 --> 02:04.410
Now let's go and move this label and put it beneath this table over here.

02:04.450 --> 02:09.690
And with that I have like a label saying this table belongs to the objects called products.

02:09.770 --> 02:13.090
Now I'm going to do the same thing for the other table over here.

02:13.090 --> 02:18.490
So I'm going to go and tag this table to the product as well, so that I can see easily which tables

02:18.490 --> 02:19.450
from the sources.

02:19.490 --> 02:22.690
This has informations about that products, business objects.

02:22.730 --> 02:23.050
All right.

02:23.090 --> 02:23.810
Now moving on.

02:23.810 --> 02:26.610
We have here a table called Customer information.

02:26.610 --> 02:28.610
So we have a lot of information about the customer.

02:28.610 --> 02:33.180
We have as well in the ERP customer information where we have the birth date and the country.

02:33.180 --> 02:35.860
So those three tables has to do with the objects.

02:35.860 --> 02:36.380
Customer.

02:36.380 --> 02:38.820
So that means we're going to go and label it like that.

02:38.820 --> 02:40.860
So let's call it customer.

02:40.860 --> 02:43.580
And I'm going to go and pick a different color for that.

02:43.620 --> 02:45.420
Let's go with the green.

02:45.420 --> 02:48.260
So I will tag this table like this.

02:48.300 --> 02:50.180
And the same thing for the other tables.

02:50.620 --> 02:54.220
So copy tag the second table and the third table.

02:54.260 --> 02:59.460
Now it is very easy for me to see which table to belong to which business objects.

02:59.460 --> 03:05.100
And now we have the final table over here, and only one table about the sales and orders in the IRB.

03:05.140 --> 03:07.100
We don't have any information about that.

03:07.100 --> 03:08.660
So this one is going to be easy.

03:08.700 --> 03:12.820
Let's call it sales and let's move it over here.

03:12.860 --> 03:17.300
And as well maybe change the color of that to for example this color over here.

03:17.340 --> 03:18.940
Now this step is very important.

03:18.940 --> 03:23.420
By building any data model in the gold layer, it gives you a big picture about the things that you

03:23.460 --> 03:24.660
are going to model.

03:24.660 --> 03:28.060
So now the next step is that we're going to go and build those objects step by step.

03:28.060 --> 03:30.780
So let's start with the first object with the customers.

03:30.780 --> 03:31.980
So here we have three tables.

03:31.980 --> 03:33.740
And we're going to start with the CRM.

03:33.740 --> 03:35.820
So let's start with this table over here.

03:35.860 --> 03:36.220
All right.

03:36.220 --> 03:39.060
So with that we know what are our business objects.

03:39.060 --> 03:40.580
And this task is done.

03:40.580 --> 03:46.100
And now in the next step we're going to go back to SQL and start doing data integrations and building

03:46.340 --> 03:47.860
completely new data model.

03:47.860 --> 03:49.180
So let's go and do that.
